.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_RAW_CHUNK_SIZE_SET 3 2026-11-03 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_raw_chunk_size_set \- configure v4 raw-MD5 chunk size
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_raw_chunk_size_set("
.BI "        mpq_patch_s *" "patch,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "raw_chunk_size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure the existing writable v4 writer before any member begins,
any successful signing setup, or finalization. Repeated calls before locking
are permitted; the last successful size wins. Member begin fixes policy even
if the member is subsequently aborted or fails. Validation rejected before
member begin, or failed signing configuration, does not falsely lock policy.
.PP
The default is 0x4000 (16 KiB). Every uint32_t value is accepted, including
zero, 1, 17 and UINT32_MAX. No power-of-two restriction applies. Zero disables
member and HET/BET trailing raw-MD5 arrays; structural MD5 is still generated.
Nonzero arrays hash exact stored bytes and exclude their own bytes from the
stored size. Empty stored members have no raw array. Processing uses bounded
buffers, not an allocation proportional to the selected chunk size; checked
layout limits can still reject a subsequent write.
.PP
Set raw size to zero before weak signing, including on MPQE output. Nonzero
raw size still rejects weak signing. Plain strong signing is supported at any
raw size; MPQE strong signing remains unsupported. Successful signing locks
raw configuration. Failed setters preserve the prior policy and do not latch
an output error. Existing terminal writer errors take precedence.
.PP
Plain and MPQE output use the same inner policy. This does not configure a
transaction: updates always preserve the source raw size. No new ownership
or lifecycle handle is introduced. Raw MD5 protects physical stored bytes;
it is separate from logical file CRC32/MD5 and signature verification.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success or a negative libmpq error code.
.SH ERRORS
Missing required pointers return LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST.
Read-only or locked handles return LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED.
Older writable generations return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. A latched terminal
writer error is returned unchanged.
